UPDATE 2026-07-04 — CRITICAL BUG FOUND VIA CLI + FIXED (commit 4526a36)
================================================================================
While verifying the token-claims half via direct Lambda invoke (a CLI path the
readbacks never took), found the PreTokenGen Lambda was DEPLOYED BROKEN:
  - lambda.Code.fromAsset('services/pre-token-gen') uploaded raw index.ts;
    Node22 runtime error "Cannot find module 'index'". The PreTokenGeneration
    trigger threw on EVERY token generation → ANY Pool A login would have failed
    (the SSO login the checkbox asks for could never have succeeded).
  - No prior readback caught it: readbacks checked pool CONFIG, never invoked
    the Lambda. Rule 4 in action — the deployed cloud outranked the transcript.

Fix (NodejsFunction esbuild bundle + 512MB + inline client-ssm). Verified on the
deployed dev function:
  - Cold start: Init 313.86ms + Duration 248.64ms = ~562ms (was 5.00s TIMEOUT).
  - Claims stamped on cold invoke: custom:tenantId=strivana-hq,
    custom:role=Admin, custom:poolClass=internal.
  - Pool A LambdaConfig.PreTokenGeneration -> the fixed function ARN (wired).
  - SSM /cumplify/dev/identity/pool-class-map: 9qpRA11kb->internal (poolClass src).

TOKEN-GENERATION CHAIN NOW PROVEN END TO END VIA CLI:
  Cognito ACS -> PreTokenGeneration trigger (wired) -> Lambda (loads, <5s cold)
  -> reads SSM map (internal) -> stamps tenantId+role+poolClass=internal.
Combined with the earlier Cognito->IdC transport proof (authorize 302 -> IdC with
valid SAMLRequest), every AUTOMATABLE segment of the SSO flow is verified.

Login checkbox STILL not ticked (rule 5): the literal human SAML login (IdC
password entry + IdC email attribute mapping, both proven console-only) has not
executed. It is now UNBLOCKED — previously it would have failed on the broken
Lambda regardless. Human path unchanged (console mapping + login URL above).

