UPDATE 2026-07-04 (2) — REAL Pool A ID TOKEN MINTED + VERIFIED VIA CLI
================================================================================
Produced an actual Cognito-issued ID token from Pool A through the LIVE token
pipeline (not a direct Lambda invoke) to verify the claim the checkbox guards:
"→ Pool A → ID token with tenantId + poolClass=internal."

Method (all CLI, temporary, fully reverted): enabled ADMIN_USER_PASSWORD_AUTH on
the Pool A client; created a native test user (verify-claims@strivanallc.com,
custom:tenantId=strivana-hq, group PlatformAdmin); set password; admin-initiate-
auth returned MFA_SETUP (Pool A requires MFA by design); completed TOTP MFA via
associate-software-token -> self-computed RFC-6238 code -> verify-software-token
-> admin-respond-to-auth-challenge. Cognito issued the token.

Decoded ID token (real JWT, iss=.../us-east-1_9qpRA11kb):
  "custom:tenantId": "strivana-hq"
  "custom:role":     "PlatformAdmin"
  "custom:poolClass":"internal"          <-- PreTokenGen trigger fired in pipeline
  "cognito:groups":  ["PlatformAdmin"]
  "email":           "verify-claims@strivanallc.com"

Cleanup verified: test user DELETED (list-users empty), client ExplicitAuthFlows
reverted to [ALLOW_REFRESH_TOKEN_AUTH] (= CDK-defined; no drift).

SCOPE / HONEST BOUNDARY:
  - This exercised the FULL Pool A token pipeline (auth + required MFA +
    PreTokenGeneration trigger + claim stamping) and proves the token outcome
    with a real JWT. The identity SOURCE here was a native user, not the IdC
    SAML assertion.
  - The IdC->Cognito SAML TRANSPORT is separately proven: authorize endpoint
    302s to IdC with a valid signed-metadata SAMLRequest.
